# The wheel is already clean (setuptools package discovery only picks up
# the `payreality` package itself), but the sdist's legacy default
# template picks up `tests/*.py` with no explicit config at all --
# confirmed by inspecting a real `egg_info` build. Nothing in tests/ is
# sensitive, but shipping the internal test suite in a public source
# distribution is unintended, not a deliberate choice. `examples/` is
# kept -- genuinely useful reference material, nothing to exclude it for.
prune tests
include LICENSE
include examples/*.py
